{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510375-can-a-malkavian-insanity-be-attenuated-somehow","id":1510375,"title":"Can a Malkavian insanity be attenuated, somehow?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-01T10:49:42-07:00","id":1510375,"title":"Can a Malkavian insanity be attenuated, somehow?","content":"From what I read, all the examples of Malkavian vampires are completely out of their mind, barely functional at best and sometimes not even that. Some, like the daughters of Ianus in Vampire - Bloodlines look reasonably sane most of the time... untill you discover they have split personality disorder.<br /> <br /> So, although I guess that many would find a &quot;sane&quot; Malkavian a self defeating idea ( they're indeed very interesting and amusing in their madness ), can you come up with some ways - both RAI and RAW - to create a Malkavian who is still in touch with reality, and somewhat able to control - or limit - his insanity?<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> Some ideas I had:<br /> <br /> 1- mabye an high Conscience, high Humanity vampire would be concerned enough with the people he could hurt due his insanity, and struggle harder to control himself<br /> 2- it seems that undead are still influenced by blood laced with alchool or drugs... mabye also psychiatric antipsychotic drugs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T11:30:04-07:00","id":1510381,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this is what you have in mind, but I always wondered about pushing the madness network a bit harder. Like, at least for the purposes of character creation, make clear that the Malkavians aren't actually just suffering random mental illnesses, they're suffering under the weight of the network pumping information into their head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T11:34:45-07:00","id":1510385,"title":"","content":"I'd say no but I have no objection to conditions which can be managed to a degree such as depression, ptsd or agoraphobia","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T11:38:39-07:00","id":1510387,"title":"","content":"I have used the idea a Malkavian who used to suffer from schizophrenia and because a mass murderer. Only after the Embrace they started to understand their disease and now they struggle really hard not to kill people. This character only drinks bagged blood and keeps a strong self discipline <br /> Another one suffers from delirium and prophetic dreams, but he has leaned to channel his visions into surrealist art. He is a regular, well behaved member of the Elysium, admired by the Toreador and whose only quirk is sometimes using cryptic sentences that nobody understands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T11:41:53-07:00","id":1510388,"title":"","content":"Look, some neurodivergences can be mitigated with medicine, so if the Malkavian consumes blood from a person who consumed the said medications, it could make sense for him to be more controlled, but that would only be temporary, and it is certain that there are Malkavian that are so crazy that you question as they haven't been destroyed yet, but there are others that despite not being normal are functional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T11:50:03-07:00","id":1510389,"title":"","content":"<i><b>&quot;The poor are crazy, the rich just eccentric&quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> Insanity is an informal, un-scientific term denoting &quot;mental instability&quot;<br /> Insanity, and madness are basically behaviors performed by certain abnormal mental or behavioral patterns. While usually it can manifest as violations of societal norms, including a person or persons becoming a danger to themselves or to other people, that is not always the case<br /> A range of mental disorders (also referred to as a mental illness) falls in to the &quot;insanity&quot; category in a sense<br /> Vampire have Malkavinas who are in the deep end, but lots of others who are Dr Hannibal LEcter or Dexter like dangerously &quot;sane&quot; to the point untill you disover they are not<br /> Anatole, the poster child of the Malkavian Clan are basically sane - or at least not worse than your avarage vampire<br /> The &quot;Dominate Malkavians&quot; are stereotyped as being more internalized and &quot;sedate&quot; (such as sociopathy, obsessive-compulsive disorder, or a tendency towards hallucination)<br /> Malkavian does not mean fishmalk. Insane does not mean unstable. Insanities come in all shapes and sizes. Many can be lived with in relative stability.<br /> From their write-up in the Revised corebook:<br /> &quot;In many cases, there's no way to tell a Malkavian apart from the &quot;sane&quot; members of other clans.&quot;<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T12:58:29-07:00","id":1510395,"title":"","content":"Devil's advocate moment:<br /> In a fixed storyline, be it a video game NPC or a written character, Malkavian madness appears as is needed to convey the essence of the character or move the story forward. In a TTRPG setting, Malkavian Madness is a game play mechanic which is supposed to have both role play implications as well as mechanical interactions.<br /> <br /> The problem is that in most of the situations where Players are running Malkavians, the madness seems to drop off when they don't want to deal with it. They will abuse the madness aspect when they want to be quirky or mess with a scene without social repercussions, but then avoid it when it would constrain their choices.<br /> <br /> Now there is a counter argument to this that in the WoD setting, if you are too non-functional, then you are simply dead. Resulting in the only surviving Malkavians being those that are just functional enough to deal with the trials of unlife. However, that sweet spot of being someone with a high functioning mental disorder is difficult for many players to balance in playstyle.<br /> <br /> The fact that Malkavians have Obfuscate as a clan discipline gives them a lot of survival leeway. But I feel that most people don't play up those aspects with malkavians. Obfuscate is how they feed, survive, interact with kindred society, and escape danger. Despite needing the discipline nearly as much as the Nosferatu, it doesn't seem to be related to their clan identity to anywhere the same degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T14:02:12-07:00","id":1510405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510375-can-a-malkavian-insanity-be-attenuated-somehow?p=1510395#post1510395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that Malkavians have Obfuscate as a clan discipline gives them a lot of survival leeway. But I feel that most people don't play up those aspects with malkavians. Obfuscate is how they feed, survive, interact with kindred society, and escape danger. Despite needing the discipline nearly as much as the Nosferatu, it doesn't seem to be related to their clan identity to anywhere the same degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not much, you can think a skill that let you diguise as anyone, can be a way to someone strange, unleast seems normal imitating the normals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T14:25:31-07:00","id":1510412,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate has many uses, but for the Malkavians I always took it as a means to blend into the background and get a good picture who and what people are around and what latest schemes are and how to best aviod them or use it to their advantage. That is how I play my Malkavian investigator in our games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T14:49:49-07:00","id":1510415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510375-can-a-malkavian-insanity-be-attenuated-somehow?p=1510405#post1510405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not much, you can think a skill that let you diguise as anyone, can be a way to someone strange, unleast seems normal imitating the normals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more along the lines of Obfuscate allowing a Malkavian to feed from sleeping mortals since their Derangements and other issues would make the social/seduction route a problem. It would allow Malks to avoid direct combat between vampires and other bad situations. Lastly the ability to be invisible and talk at people is a great way of sharing the madness without needing to use Dementation.<br /> <br /> As for how Obfuscate *** helps a Malkavian, there are a few ways to use it. In one game the Malkavian player used Obfuscate rank three to project a different outside appearance when a different personality took over. In another game we had an obsessed Malkavian who would use Obfuscate rank three to look like a different person every time the target saw them, but every projection had something that was bright red, the lipstick, a scarf, baseball cap, etc. so the target knew something was deeply wrong.<br /> <br /> Lastly back when Malkavians gots switched over to Dementation rather than Dominate, Obfuscate could assist in pulling off similar tricks. Rather than using Dominate to make the target falsely remember doing something or programing them to do that out of character thing, the Malkavian just uses Obfuscate *** to pose as them and cause the collateral damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T15:39:48-07:00","id":1510426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510375-can-a-malkavian-insanity-be-attenuated-somehow?p=1510415#post1510415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking more along the lines of Obfuscate allowing a Malkavian to feed from sleeping mortals since their Derangements and other issues would make the social/seduction route a problem. It would allow Malks to avoid direct combat between vampires and other bad situations. Lastly the ability to be invisible and talk at people is a great way of sharing the madness without needing to use Dementation.<br /> <br /> As for how Obfuscate *** helps a Malkavian, there are a few ways to use it. In one game the Malkavian player used Obfuscate rank three to project a different outside appearance when a different personality took over. In another game we had an obsessed Malkavian who would use Obfuscate rank three to look like a different person every time the target saw them, but every projection had something that was bright red, the lipstick, a scarf, baseball cap, etc. so the target knew something was deeply wrong.<br /> <br /> Lastly back when Malkavians gots switched over to Dementation rather than Dominate, Obfuscate could assist in pulling off similar tricks. Rather than using Dominate to make the target falsely remember doing something or programing them to do that out of character thing, the Malkavian just uses Obfuscate *** to pose as them and cause the collateral damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking more as a concept I've never had a chance to play as a Malkavian so it's not like I get to try out many tricks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T15:43:37-07:00","id":1510427,"title":"","content":"It does help to actually look at the mechanics of Derangements, since their fidelity to the reality of mental health conditions is minimal.<br /> <br /> This makes building a high-functioning Malkavian easier: since basically what you want is high Virtues, and high Willpower. While each is unique, most Derangements are either resisted by Virtues or Willpower, or penalize them in some fashion. Merits like Code of Honor, Calm Heart, and Lucky are also useful to help resist or mitigate the mechanics of most Derangements.<br /> <br /> While the mechanics are generally harsh enough that you can't just ignore Derangements even with getting 5s in all your Virtues, Willpower 10, and the Merits above, you can heavily reduce how often they manifest in a noticeable fashion to others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T16:31:34-07:00","id":1510439,"title":"","content":"IDK if this is something you would want, but I have had the idea of a combo discipline with Dominate 5 and auspex 4 to perhaps temporarily give their insanity to someone else. I wanted it to act in a similar fashion to animalism 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T18:38:24-07:00","id":1510447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510375-can-a-malkavian-insanity-be-attenuated-somehow?p=1510427#post1510427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does help to actually look at the mechanics of Derangements, since their fidelity to the reality of mental health conditions is minimal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I just say that I find the way RPGs treat mental illness? The only time I really like it is in Unknown Armies, and that's because in 3e your mental state is the core of your character. In VtM it feels mostly like they're slapped on to increase the 'horror' elements without any actual care, and nWoD1e felt even worse in that regard.<br /> <br /> <br /> Although let's be honest, from a verisimilitude perspective any Malkavian who is mad as a hatter, old, and alive is probably playing up their madness. Most Malkavians should be high functioning and Bloodlines is actually a good example of this (the Primogen has a relatively unobtrusive obsession with reason, Voreman's issues are mostly their feud with themself, and the Malk PC is definitely playing the loon). Let them spend Willpower to function when needed, but also don't hesitate to call for Willpower if they're being too lax in roleplaying it.<br /> <br /> As a side note, I'd love it if pre-V5 Dementation could be more tailored to a Mall's individual madness, but I understand that it's already a pretty narrow Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T18:54:49-07:00","id":1510449,"title":"","content":"The clanbook notes that those Malkavians who are barely functional, screaming lunatics usually get put down by their sire or other vampires because of the obvious threat they pose to the Masquerade. This creates a system of &quot;(un)natural&quot; selection&quot; in which Malkavians in Camarilla cities are the ones who can function well, at least to the point of not posing a threat to the Masquerade. Those who can't do that get killed shortly after being turned into a vampire. <br /> <br /> Also remember that there are some Malkavians where their derangement is obvious. On the other hand there are Malkavians whose derangement is less obvious. There are even Malkavians (like Dr. Netchurch) who don't even realize that they're insane and don't even really identify with the Clan. &quot;Oh, I'm not crazy like those guys.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T11:37:54-07:00","id":1510503,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about a Malkavian who's deeply unhappy with his madness, and try every possible way - including heavy medications - to suppress it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T12:14:52-07:00","id":1510506,"title":"","content":"I've seen a Maalkavian concept that lost track of reality and tried to inflict pain on himself constantly to know what was real and I don't know if it works in reality, he believes so, but there are times when he himself doubts it. It's good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T12:27:43-07:00","id":1510510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510375-can-a-malkavian-insanity-be-attenuated-somehow?p=1510381#post1510381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if this is what you have in mind, but I always wondered about pushing the madness network a bit harder. Like, at least for the purposes of character creation, make clear that the Malkavians aren't actually just suffering random mental illnesses, they're suffering under the weight of the network pumping information into their head.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair is that some of them are not tightly connected to the Madness Network such as Dr. Netchurch who is said to have weak ties to it and I play my Malkavian with that in mind. He might hear the stray thought or so or feels a hunch from time to time. But that is extent of my character's connection to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T12:43:12-07:00","id":1510517,"title":"","content":"Most Malkavians aren't happy about their Clan's curse... but given it's supernatural origins, most have just accepted it and desire to cope with it the best they can. Even with real world mental health conditions &quot;suppression&quot; isn't a realistic goal. Drugs, therapy, and so on are tools to help making the coping process less burdensome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T12:49:53-07:00","id":1510518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510375-can-a-malkavian-insanity-be-attenuated-somehow?p=1510439#post1510439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IDK if this is something you would want, but I have had the idea of a combo discipline with Dominate 5 and auspex 4 to perhaps temporarily give their insanity to someone else. I wanted it to act in a similar fashion to animalism 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a distrubing amalgam power and I wonder what kind of humanity loss you would suffer? I hope you show it to us later as it sounds interesting to say the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T14:05:12-07:00","id":1510522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510375-can-a-malkavian-insanity-be-attenuated-somehow?p=1510518#post1510518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be a distrubing amalgam power and I wonder what kind of humanity loss you would suffer? I hope you show it to us later as it sounds interesting to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Malkav's Gift<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Dominate 5, Auspex 4<br /> <br /> Description: Malkav's Gift is a unique power that enables a Malkavian vampire to transfer their derangements to another individual temporarily.<br /> <br /> System: To use Malkav's Gift, the Malkavian rolls Manipulation + Empathy (Difficulty 6). Each success achieved on the roll extends the duration of the loaned derangement by one hour.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be surprised if a vampire who constantly uses this eventually falls to the beast, its less dangerous for vampires who follow a path. Interestingly, while making this power I discovered that Chat GPT works better than Grammarly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T14:10:04-07:00","id":1510523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510375-can-a-malkavian-insanity-be-attenuated-somehow?p=1510503#post1510503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about a Malkavian who's deeply unhappy with his madness, and try every possible way - including heavy medications - to suppress it.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Martinelli's Ring of Clear Thought</b>\u200b is what you need from the '92 Players Guide to the Sabbat<br /> It is gold ring was the property of a Malkavian elder destroyed during the Anarch Revolt. A ghoul created it for her as a gift. Wearing the ring removes all fears, phobias, derangements, and any mental flaws the individual wearing the ring might have. Removing the ring brings them back twice as strong, and the wearer becomes obsessed with recovering it.<br /> <br /> Or find a Salubri Healer, they have a history to tend the Malkavians like how Saulot tended his brother Malkav (finding an Unicorn is hard, but a great source of story - in the last desperate attempt hunting a near extinct bloodline member - with all the attached problems this may cause<br /> <br /> <b>Obeah</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Mens Sana </b>(Vampire Storytellers Companion)<br /> With this power, the Salubri can heal madness, quieting inner demons and bringing a soul to peace. Indeed, ancient stories of the Salubri state that Saulot used this power to bring sweet, if temporary, relief to his \u201cbrother\u201d Malkav. Other, more recent stories claim that Saulot caused Malkav\u2019s madness in the first place.<br /> <b>System:</b> The player spends two blood points and rolls Intelligence + Empathy (difficulty 8). The use of Mens Sana takes at least 10 minutes of relatively uninterrupted conversation. Success cures the subject of one derangement of the Salubri player\u2019s choice. This power cannot cure a Malkavian of his core derangement, though it alleviates its effects for the rest of the scene. A botch inflicts the same derangement on the Salubri for the rest of the scene<br /> <br /> <b>Obeah</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u200b<br /> <b>Treat the Sick Mind</b> (The Vampire Players Guide (1991) and The Vampire Players Guide 2nd ed (1993))<br /> The vampire may cure a derangement of a target. If she first made a roll to sense the derangement, each success on that roll grants an extra die on the roll to cure the derangement. When the vampire uses this power, her third eye and the target both glow in gold light.<br /> <b>System:</b> Sensing the Derangement requires a Perception + Empathy roll (difficulty 7). Remember, the Derangement is a survival mechanism and the subconscious will not be willing to let it go. Curing the Derangement requires Charisma + Medicine roll (difficulty Willpower + 3) During the cure, the vampire gets one extra die to roll for every success made on the diagnosis. During the treatment, the target's body is bathed in a soft golden glow from the third eye, and anyone in the area will more than likely notice both the glow and the eye. Also, if the target moves during this time, the difficulty of both the diagnosis and the treatment increases by one. If the target moves more than five feet away from the healer, the treatment ends.<br /> <br /> <b>Valeren</b> (Healer Path) \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>The Ailing Spirit</b> (Dark Ages Companion and Dark Ages Storytellers Companion)<br /> Mischievous demons of madness plague many souls in the Dark medieval era, but Cainites, due to their unholy nature and dastardly activities, are among the most frequent victims of madness. By invoking The Ailing Spirit, a Salubri can briefly drive off the demons that cause insane fits, and bring a subject to lucidity. This ability even works on Malkavians (albeit temporarily), for it is said that gentle Salout himself was the first to use The Ailing spirit - on his brother, Malkav. Some Cainites - not all of them under the sway of the Tremere and their allies - hear legends that Saulot used this ability to enslave his beloved brother for a time. Using this power on mortals know to be mad may attract the attention of the local Church, so the kind-hearted Salubri is warned against pursuing demons of madness too fervently.<br /> <b>System:</b> The player spends two blood points and rolls Intelligence + Empathy (difficulty 8). Success indicates that the character has cured one of the subject's Derangements. Failure means she cannot try again that night, and a botch pulls the Derangement from the subject onto the Salubri's own psyche for the rest of the night. This ability is subject to certain limitations. First, the character cannot use it on himself; one's own demons are too slippery to grasp. Second, it can only be used once per night on a given subject. Finally, it cannot heal the permanent Derangements of a Malkavian. It can provide a Malkavian with a scene's worth of lucidity, however.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>But I think it is the part of the personal horror if a Malkavian self-aware and &quot;sane&quot; enough to know his insanity and try to find a &quot;cure&quot; - of course without a hope to succeed</b></u><br /> Dr. James Alfred Kennedy, or better known as Dr. James Kennedy, was the main antagonist of Dame Agatha Christie's posthumously-released 1976 novel Sleeping Murder: Miss Marple's Last Case, or simply known as Sleeping Murder, which is Dame Christie's final published novel and the finale of Miss Marple series.<br /> Dr. James Kennedy is the half-brother of the story's primary victim, Helen Halliday, and the step-uncle of her step-daughter, Gwenda. It was revealed that Helen never actually ran away from her husband and step-daughter. In fact, Helen was murdered by her own half-brother, Dr. James Kennedy, who had developed an one-sided feeling of twisted love and attempted to have an incestuous relationship with her. However, Helen married her later husband and tried to leave her twisted brother.<br /> <b>He became a Psychiatrist to understand his own mental illness and cure himself</b><br /> Medice, cura te ipsum; Physician, heal thyself!<br /> Of course he never achieved his goal like how a Malkavian never can be free from the Clan's Curse<br /> But it not mean a Malkavian can't try... but even if somehow a Malkavian would find a way to cure/supress the derangement he have, the Madness is in their Blood, and their mind is connected via the Maddness Network... so I would be a cruel DM and simply another derangement would blossom in place of the &quot;cured&quot; one...<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-02-2023, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T11:22:31-07:00","id":1510623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510375-can-a-malkavian-insanity-be-attenuated-somehow#post1510375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I read, all the examples of Malkavian vampires are completely out of their mind, barely functional at best and sometimes not even that. Some, like the daughters of Ianus in Vampire - Bloodlines look reasonably sane most of the time... untill you discover they have split personality disorder.<br /> <br /> So, although I guess that many would find a &quot;sane&quot; Malkavian a self defeating idea ( they're indeed very interesting and amusing in their madness ), can you come up with some ways - both RAI and RAW - to create a Malkavian who is still in touch with reality, and somewhat able to control - or limit - his insanity?<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> Some ideas I had:<br /> <br /> 1- mabye an high Conscience, high Humanity vampire would be concerned enough with the people he could hurt due his insanity, and struggle harder to control himself<br /> 2- it seems that undead are still influenced by blood laced with alchool or drugs... mabye also psychiatric antipsychotic drugs?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is the option of asking a Mage - including a Tradition Mage ( for example an Ecstatic or a Verbenae Sorceress ) or a Technocrat ( for example a Progenitor or a Technomancer from the Syndicate ) for help. This can lead to good and positive outcomes even when the situation and results will be that the help for the Malkavian Kindred will be slight, partial, or temporary.<br /> <br /> Other Malkavians - and of course also Malkavian Ghouls - could definitely give definite, particular, optimistic, and good support. It is clear that team effort and group cooperation is an area where Malkavian Vampires tend to achieve victories and successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T08:02:47-07:00","id":1510703,"title":"","content":"I like Malks as divided mostly between -slightly off all the time- and -very crazy on rare occasions-. <br /> <br /> The Beast doesn't exist to fuck with you, it's there to keep you alive. Clan curses aren't there to fuck you, they're their to push you in certain directions and facilitate cooperation with the clan. So with that in mind the madness shouldn't drive you to suicide or be worse than other clan weaknesses. Every other clan can build themselves around their weakness, mitigating it's detriments, and the malkavians should be no exception. Malks can learn to avoid their triggers and build their strategies,abilities and backgrounds to mitigate constant-effect ailments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T09:38:26-07:00","id":1510707,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem, again, goes back to the underlying systems. The Derangements themselves are all over the place in terms of what their effects are, and to cope with them.<br /> <br /> Every Brujah is more prone to Frenzy, but this mechanic is consistent for all of them even if you do something to add some personal flavor to it. If you want to avoid a gather of Brujah, or with a few Brujah in it, to avoid getting derailed by Frenzies, the same basic strategies can be applied with only minimal adjustments for individuals.<br /> <br /> The Malkavians are a grab bag because of their mechanics. Every Malkavian you add to a mix exponentially increases the difficulty of avoiding triggering Derangements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T16:35:24-07:00","id":1510732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510375-can-a-malkavian-insanity-be-attenuated-somehow?p=1510707#post1510707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem, again, goes back to the underlying systems. The Derangements themselves are all over the place in terms of what their effects are, and to cope with them.<br /> <br /> Every Brujah is more prone to Frenzy, but this mechanic is consistent for all of them even if you do something to add some personal flavor to it. If you want to avoid a gather of Brujah, or with a few Brujah in it, to avoid getting derailed by Frenzies, the same basic strategies can be applied with only minimal adjustments for individuals.<br /> <br /> The Malkavians are a grab bag because of their mechanics. Every Malkavian you add to a mix exponentially increases the difficulty of avoiding triggering Derangements.</div> </div> </div> </div>In many cases where there is an increased difficulty or a specific problematic factors, there is also a distinct chance for earning and receiving positive rewards and going through good experiences. Honest effort can lead to perfect outcomes and results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T16:43:43-07:00","id":1510733,"title":"","content":"Without getting to how that can apply to reality, or even good role-playing, where do the mechanics back that up for playing Malkavians and using them in play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T17:39:27-07:00","id":1510741,"title":"","content":"Something to throw in here: Some madness, but be still functional as has been mentioned. A real world example would be Emperor Norton I.<br /> An example in game was from a chronicle I ran were the malkavian was paranoid, but could still go about his night to night in LA. It just so happened that LA was a city in Vietnam and when his madness got really bad he started seeing the coteries enemies as VC, but he could still distinguish friend from foe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T16:15:25-07:00","id":1510834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510375-can-a-malkavian-insanity-be-attenuated-somehow?p=1510741#post1510741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to throw in here: Some madness, but be still functional as has been mentioned. A real world example would be Emperor Norton</div> </div> </div> </div>Any other historical persons or fictional characters that you associate with Malkavian Vampires or with Malkavian Ghouls to a significant and considerable extent ? Ideas or examples from other RPG games ( like Pathfinder or Dungeons and Dragons ) and computer games would be interesting and good to hear and read about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T23:46:35-07:00","id":1510863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510375-can-a-malkavian-insanity-be-attenuated-somehow?p=1510834#post1510834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any other historical persons or fictional characters that you associate with Malkavian Vampires or with Malkavian Ghouls to a significant and considerable extent ? Ideas or examples from other RPG games ( like Pathfinder or Dungeons and Dragons ) and computer games would be interesting and good to hear and read about.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to get dark there's Charles Manson. Oh, Howard Hughes Jr. The man had some serious issues in his life. <br /> <br /> As far as fictional characters... There's the nordic king of Skyrim, Borgas, who outlawed death and anyone relating to Sheogorath would work as good inspiration. <br /> <br /> From Pathfinder there's a sunny kuthite cleric named Laori Vaus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T01:17:50-07:00","id":1510963,"title":"","content":"Some quests, characters, concepts, and stories from Skyrim could definitely be good and positive in regard to coming up with and developing ideas about Malkavian Vampires and Malkavian Ghouls.<br /> <br /> For example theories and ideas about their inclinations and attitudes in regard to emotions, feelings, dreams, ambitions, events and situations.<br /> <br /> Do you know any Pathfinder supplements or books that you would rate or recommend as appropriate for a good, normal, standard, and positive \u200breading - and also introduction, understanding, and exploration - of this role-playing setting and game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T23:56:44-07:00","id":1511051,"title":"","content":"My two cents, and how I've run Malks:<br /> <br /> First, there are a lot more &quot;failed&quot; Malkavians than people realize, but the Malkavians tend to clean up their own messes. When a Malk gets permission to embrace, it's an open secret that they will kill the offspring if it becomes too broken to ever function in polite society, then try again until it comes out right. The Malkavians we see on Elysium are the ones that came out halfway decent. They're the survivors, and their childer will be judged by the same standard, perpetuating the cycle.<br /> <br /> Second, Malkavians that survive aren't dumb. They know perfectly well that the rest of the world doesn't think like they do. They have learned to hide their truth, because the alternative is burning. They develop coping strategies to survive in a world that behaves in ways their mind doesn't compute, and to hide the worst of it.<br /> <br /> Just look at real neurodivergent people and psychiatry patients. They can become phenomenal actors and liars, pretending that everything is fine when it is clearly not <br /> Eventually, for the Malkavian, things inevitably boil over and they go &quot;full Malkavian&quot; for a bit, before they &quot;calm down&quot; aka put the mask back on so that society will tolerate them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Furthermore, I believe Carthage should be destroyed.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23835-pang4","name":"pang4","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T00:32:36-07:00","id":1511055,"title":"","content":"Indeed<br /> Many like to think, a Malkavian is like the Joker from Batman... but the Joker - while could be cold, calculating, dangerously sane if needed and could reinvent his own sanity and personality on a whim - is actually a Malkavian Antitribu &quot;stereotype&quot;<br /> A Camarilla Malkavian is more like Bruce Wayne; good old Bruce have more than a few derangement (to the point he even have the &quot;Zur-En-Arrh&quot; persona is a backup personality created by Bruce Wayne in the event he was ever mentally compromised...) and just as fragile and mentally unstable as the Joker. He has just as many toys and is just as keen on playing dress up. He just happens to fight for the good side...<br /> But totally could function as Bruce Wayne - aka. a Malkavian in an Elysium or a polite Camarilla or Human society<br /> The scary thing is, the Joker is as much capable to do so (and do it when it suits his needs and plans) just decided not to...\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T01:27:00-07:00","id":1511056,"title":"","content":"Or if we thin kabout it, there is a better example of &quot;functioning&quot; Malkavians...<br /> Somewhere at the top of the forest a little boy and his bear play. Sadly, the forest is not, in fact, a place of enchantment, but rather one of disenchantment, where neurodevelopmental and psychosocial problems go unrecognized and untreated...<br /> Lets begin with Pooh. This unfortunate bear embodies the concept of comorbidity. Most striking is his Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD), inattentive subtype, but Pooh might also demonstrate significant impulsivity, as witnessed, for example, by his poorly thought out attempt to get honey by disguising himself as a rain cloud, witch is reflected more on his comorbid cognitive impairment, further aggravated by an obsessive fixation on honey as an Impulsive eating disorder.\u200b The latter, of course, has also contributed to his significant obesity. Pooh's perseveration on food and his repetitive counting behaviours raise the diagnostic possibility of Obsessive Compulsive Disorder (OCD). Given his coexisting ADHD and OCD, we could question whether Pooh may over time present with Tourette's syndrome. Pooh is also clearly described as having Very Little Brain. The cause of Pooh's poor brain growth may be found in the stories themselves. Early on we see Pooh being dragged downstairs bump, bump, bump, on the back of his head. Could his later cognitive struggles be the result of a type of Shaken Bear Syndrome?<br /> And what of little Piglet? Poor, anxious, blushing, flustered little Piglet. He clearly suffers from a Generalized Anxiety Disorder. Piglet is in a perpetual state of worry and can often be heard saying &quot;Oh, dear.&quot; He has also developed an ear twitch, common in overly anxious individuals.<br /> Pooh and Piglet are at risk for additional self-esteem injury because of the chronic dysthymia of their neighbour, Eeyore. What a sad life that donkey lives. Thanks to his Depressive disorder, he always has a bleak outlook on life, and never feels any positive emotions like happiness and excitement.<br /> Poor old Owl, have Dyslexia and narcissistic personality disorder. While he is exceptionally bright, it is frequently shown that Owl has trouble reading. An example would be in <i>Pooh\u2019s Grand Adventure</i> when he mistakes the word school for &quot;skull.&quot; Owl is also theorized to have narcissism, an inflated sense of self-importance, due to his belief that he is wiser than the others.\u200bHis poignant attempts to cover up for his phonological deficits are similar to what we see day in and day out in others so afflicted.<br /> Kanga have Social anxiety disorder and she is very overprotective of her son, and she would never let her son make his own decisions because of her overprotectiveness.\u200b<br /> As for her son, Roo? It is not his impulsivity or hyperactivity that is concerning, those are probably age appropriate. Bu he probably have <i>A</i>utism spectrum disorder.He lacks awareness of danger and has a strange attachment to sitting in his mother's pouch...<br /> \u200bTigger is gregarious and affectionate, but he has a recurrent pattern of risk-taking behaviours. With the mildest of provocation he tries honey, haycorns and even thistles - example of his impulsive sampling of unknown substances when he first comes to the Hundred Acre Wood. Tigger has no knowledge of the potential outcome of his experimentation. Later we find him climbing tall trees and acting in a way that can only be described as socially intrusive. He leads Roo into danger. His Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD) also clear; Tigger is always seen bouncing and can never stay in one place for a long period of time.<br /> Finally, there is Rabbit. You can note his tendency to be extraordinarily self-important and his odd belief system that he has a great many relations (many of other species!) and friends. He seems to have an overriding need to organize others, often against their will, into new groupings, with himself always at the top of the reporting structure. But his Obsessive Compulsive Disorder (OCD) also manifests; Rabbit is very orderly and obsessive, mostly with regard to his garden.<br /> And all on the top of that, there is Christopher Robin. It is believed that all of the talking animal characters above are manifested depending on Christopher's mood; he is suffering from Schizophrenia (and E.H. Shepard's illustrations suggest possible future gender identity issues for this child) not to mention you can note in the stories early signs of difficulty with academics \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> BUT against all of these... the Asylum of Hundred Acre Woods is a functioning society<br /> They have their issues, but capable to work together, be and have friends - not to mention tolerating each other and other's problems - and <b><i>without </i></b>any medications or professional treatment!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T08:14:37-07:00","id":1524139,"title":"","content":"Mostly I interpret Malkavians using my own neuroatypias or some of close friends. On a second way I go full fishmalk on the surface and use a sociopathy or depression on the core. About the alleviation of symptoms, the safest bet would be a Salubri, or a very high willpower.<br /> Mechanically is a mess. Most of the games don't really understand mental impairments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T14:42:32-07:00","id":1524152,"title":"","content":"There's an important distinction. &quot;Madness&quot; is not the same as &quot;insane&quot;. Malkavians have a permanent Derangement (meaning that in terms of game mechanics, it will always be on the character sheet and cannot be overcome and eliminated). That is not the same as insanity. Insanity is a legal, not a medical definition. It means the person cannot be held responsible for their actions. It could be the result of a mental illness, but it could a result of dementia, brain damage, or some other factor. Plenty of people suffer from some form of mental illness, but would never be considered insane or even mad. It's really up to the ST and players how they intend to portray their Malkavian NPCs and PCs.<br /> <br /> Obviously some derangements seem more like crazy than others. But many derangements are things that people around you could tolerate, or even may not notice about you. A Malkavian with Bipolar Disorder might not be pleasant to be around when her mood swings happen, but those mood swings could be tolerable. And the Malkavian character can always choose to spend Willpower to suppress it. A Malkavian with the bulimia derangement, if she keeps it secret, might even be seen as completely normal. Unless you happen to witness their overfeeding and subsequent burning of their blood points so they can feed again, what would seem out of the ordinary about them? <br /> <br /> Some derangements are just less noticeable than others. Some derangements seem less crazy than others. People usually want a really noticeable derangement like Paranoia, Schizophrenia, Megalomania, and Fugue. Some may make a Malkavian actually psychotic. But what if you make the Malkavian a highly functioning sociopath who can hide his utter lack of empathy? Or a Malkavian who suffers from depression?<br /> <br /> A Malkavian who actively &quot;fights&quot; his Derangement just needs to spend (and regain) a lot of temporary Willpower. Of course, any Malkavian who does that is considered low on the totem pole in the Malkavian clan. Their clan status depends on vampires accepting their Derangement and using it in ways to see past the conventional view of reality into actual insights in what the world is &quot;really&quot; like.<br /> <br /> Personally, when I run chronicles as an ST I like to provide a wide spectrum of Malkavian concepts. Highly functioning to complete screw ups that will need to be destroyed to protect the Masquerade, from people who appear very sane to those acting in ways that everybody else finds crazy. The difficult thing is making the characters feel like they actually as vampires, and not just someone's stupid idea for a Chaotic Neutral character in D&amp;D that exists just to annoy people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-17T12:18:08-07:00","id":1524203,"title":"","content":"I play my Malkavian as someone suffering with a Obessive need to learn secrets and it can get him into trouble and is aware of it and tries to keep that in check and his coterie that he is part of also keeps that in mind and try to ground him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}